--- !u!114 &3964474612698384654
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 8327429281612440629}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1fd0f65fa6943480dbe17682591d3d2c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  cueName: T13_Entry
  mode: 0
  entryTitle: Wechsel zu VR
  entryHighlight: VR
  entryReason: Um dir das Chemielabor anzuschauen
  arrivalTitle: "Hast du Fragen \xFCber den Kontext, in dem du dich gerade befindest?"
  arrivalHighlight: 
  arrivalReason: 
  waitingText: Ich warte auf deine Frage
  listeningText: "Ich h\xF6re zu\u2026"
  thinkingText: Sammle Antworten
  enterLabel: Enter VR
  dismissLabel: Jetzt nicht
  closeLabel: "Schlie\xDFen"
  assistantNote: You are an ENTRY cue shown before the user enters the target context.
  contextText: "# Target context: a VR representation of the chemistry lab\r\n\r\nThis
    is the knowledge the cue may draw on. Answer ONLY from what is written here.\r\n(Written
    in English; if the user speaks German, answer in German.)\r\n\r\n## The situation\r\n\r\nThe
    user is walking through the building in AR, on the way to a lecture room. A message
    just arrived from Peter, asking how many working stations there are in the chemistry
    lab. As the user walks a few meters further, an entry cue appears to their right
    \u2014 right in front of the real chemistry lab room. The cue offers a way to
    look inside the lab **without entering the real room**.\r\n\r\n## What you can
    transition into\r\n\r\nA **virtual representation (a VR clone) of the chemistry
    lab** \u2014 the same room that is physically to the user's right. It is a faithful
    copy of the real lab: the layout, the working stations, and where things are
    placed all match reality. Stepping in lets the user take a peek and walk around
    the lab virtually.\r\n\r\n## Why the virtual version instead of the real room\r\n\r\n-
    The user cannot / does not want to enter the real room right now.\r\n- People
    are currently working in the real lab; the virtual visit avoids interrupting
    them.\r\n- In the virtual representation the user is **alone** \u2014 free to
    look around at their own pace.\r\n\r\n## What's in the lab\r\n\r\n- The lab is
    laid out with a number of working stations plus the usual equipment; it is a
    compact, straightforward space.\r\n- Do NOT state how many working stations there
    are \u2014 you don't have that number. If the user asks how many, tell them that's
    exactly what stepping inside lets them see and count for themselves.\r\n- The
    chemistry lab is located in **building 64, on the ground floor**.\r\n\r\n## How
    you move and interact inside\r\n\r\n- Move around by **teleporting with the right
    controller** \u2014 point where you want to go and teleport there.\r\n- You can
    freely look around and walk through the space to see how the lab is set up and
    where everything is.\r\n- There are no tasks to complete inside \u2014 it is
    purely for looking and getting oriented.\r\n\r\n## The transition itself\r\n\r\n-
    **Entering is quick:** joining takes about a second, with a short preview animation
    as you come in from the side.\r\n- **Time inside:** finding what you need takes
    only about two minutes (at most two to five).\r\n- **Going back is easy:** an
    exit cue lets you leave the virtual lab and return to AR. There are no extra
    steps and no additional tasks.\r\n- **No interruption:** when you return, you
    simply continue the navigation task you were doing before \u2014 nothing you
    were doing is lost.\r\n"
  cards:
  - id: preview
    kind: 0
    title: PREVIEW
    caption: Das Chemielabor, das du betrittst
    image: {fileID: 0}
    video: {fileID: 0}
    bodyText: 
    whenToShow: Show when the user asks what the lab looks like or to see/preview
      it.
  - id: interact
    kind: 1
    title: VIDEO
    caption: "Bewegung \xB7 Teleport"
    image: {fileID: 0}
    video: {fileID: 0}
    bodyText: 
    whenToShow: Show when the user asks how to move or interact (teleport, controllers).
  - id: navigate
    kind: 2
    title: Orientierung
    caption: 
    image: {fileID: 0}
    video: {fileID: 0}
    bodyText: "1. Ziel anschauen, zum Teleportieren greifen.\n2. Rechten Stick tippen
      zum Drehen.\n3. Umschauen, um die Arbeitspl\xE4tze zu finden."
    whenToShow: Show when the user asks how to get around or orient inside.
